<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20958] FLR-ECRO: lseek(SEEK_DATA/SEEK_HOLE) blocks on EC file with unavailable OST</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20958</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lseek(fd, off, SEEK_DATA)&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;SEEK_HOLE&lt;/tt&gt; on an EC file in RDONLY state with a data stripe on an unavailable (unmounted, failing over) OST block in &lt;tt&gt;ll_lseek()&lt;/tt&gt; (CIT_LSEEK) until the OST returns, even though reads of the same file are rebuilt from parity without delay.  See the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20212" title="FLR-ECRO: verify non-write RPCs do not block client " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20212"&gt;LU-20212&lt;/a&gt; test results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;osc_lock_enqueue &amp;lt; cl_lock_enqueue &amp;lt; lov_lock_enqueue &amp;lt; cl_lock_enqueue &amp;lt; cl_lock_request &amp;lt; cl_io_lock &amp;lt; cl_io_loop &amp;lt; ll_lseek &amp;lt; ll_file_seek
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;64086 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12668" title="FLR-EC: resync parity components" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12668"&gt;LU-12668&lt;/a&gt;) handles an OST that is deactivated (-ESHUTDOWN) but not one that is down and still active, which waits in the enqueue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reporting the whole extent of an unavailable stripe as data is always correct for &lt;tt&gt;SEEK_DATA&lt;/tt&gt;/&lt;tt&gt;SEEK_HOLE&lt;/tt&gt;, so the lseek could use a no-delay enqueue and treat an unavailable stripe that way (or use the parity stripes' extents) instead of waiting for the OST.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
